  "copy": "<span class=\"dl\">BHUBANESWAR:</span> Akvan has strengthened into a severe cyclonic storm over the Bay of Bengal and is likely to cross the coast between Narsapur in Andhra Pradesh and Puri in Odisha, close to Gopalpur, by Friday noon or afternoon. Winds of 90 to 100 km/h, gusting to 110, are expected as it makes landfall. About 72,000 people have been moved to safety across eastern India, and the Railways has rescheduled three trains. Kolkata and Gangetic West Bengal are under a heavy-rain warning, with very heavy rain likely at isolated places on Friday. Across the bay, about 1,000 tourists are stranded on Bangladesh’s St Martin’s Island as boats stay off the sea.",
